    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by the explosive potential of **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.22). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor bump against Sonny Gray, and his dynamic platoon advantage pushes him into elite territory despite a respectable opposing arm. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** exploits a favorable matchup against Seth Lugo, with a strong 14% boost derived from the SP\u2019s xERA, making him an essential start. While **Heliot Ramos** (63.60) and **Luis Lara** (59.60) are not top-tier power hitters, their strong scores are buoyed by advantageous matchups against weak opposing starters (Robbie Ray and Andrew Abbott), providing the depth required to sustain our 5x5 metrics.\n\nStrategic roster management remains focused on maximizing stolen base potential and efficient matchups. **Miguel Vargas** (50.01) is a critical inclusion today; while his score is modest, the combination of a high xwOBA and a slow SP delivery from Bradley offers an sneaky opportunity for an SB\u2014a vital asset for our scarcity-driven strategy. On the bench, **Wade Meckler** (41.54) was the most difficult exclusion. While his 3rd-order placement in his respective lineup was appealing, the overall efficiency of our starting OF unit, particularly the platoon-advantaged **Heliot Ramos**, ultimately superseded him. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, as their continued absence remains a significant drag on our ceiling.\n\nA note of caution regarding our battery: **Drake Baldwin** (49.97) and **Liam Hicks** (41.19) are facing elite arms in Wheeler and deGrom, respectively. Their scores are heavily deflated by the SP skill disadvantage, effectively capping their upside today. We are starting them to maintain games played, but fantasy managers should adjust expectations for their offensive contributions. With no major weather alerts impacting our slate, the focus remains on leveraging the favorable SP xERA ratings of Abbott and Ray to boost our mid-tier hitters into productive territory.",
